# Keep the working tree clean: force LF in the repo and let git restore CRLF on
# checkout, so the same files do not show up as modified on Windows.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# ── Development-only files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are tracked on purpose: the regression suites in dev_tests/ are how the
# behaviour below was verified, and they must stay runnable from a fresh clone.
#
# They are hidden from `git archive`, which is what a release tarball and most
# "download the repo" flows are built from. The tests still work for anyone who
# clones the repository; they just do not ship inside a packaged release.
dev_tests/ export-ignore

# Internal handoff notes for the development line, not user documentation.
HANDOFF.md export-ignore
